{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791004660,"nonce":"Fk8rRgpx5KxhQQ4dvdM+hjsSWF8=","title":"osr_retier forced_snapshots never takes the re-tier hand-off on macOS","message":"`crates/ash_cli/tests/osr_retier.rs::forced_snapshots_from_ordinary_and_osr_entries_preserve_live_state` fails on macOS arm64 at the hybrid step: \"hybrid, plain=0 never took the intended compiled hand-off\". The answer is right; the path the test pins is not taken.\n\nCommand (the test's own arguments):\n\n    ASH_OSR=1 ASH_CL_RETIER=1 ASH_TEST_RETIER_AFTER=4096 ASH_OSR_LOG=1 ASH_RETIER_TEST_PLAIN=0 \\\n      ash --mode hybrid --jit-threshold 1 --opt-threshold 10000 crates/ash/test/tests/test_retier_snapshot.hl\n\n- Mac, 5aa28fd and 140d29d alike, 3/3 runs each: `[osr] entering findex=261 pc=15 ...` and no `[retier] taken` line.\n- NUC (x86_64 Linux), 3/3: `[osr] entering findex=261 ...` then `[retier] taken layout=2 source=osr`.\n\nSo it predates today's commits and is platform-specific. Until c822ee5's part 1 (140d29d) the test never reached this step on the Mac: its interp step timed out first (3M throws at ~40 us each against a 120 s limit).\n\nBoth platforms log `defer findex=261 tier=llvm reason=handed-off`, then a later promote with `staged 1 entry for findex=261 ahead of its promote`. Next: find out which entry the Mac interpreter enters (Cranelift OSR or the staged LLVM one), and whether the Cranelift entry's re-tier poll runs under `ASH_TEST_RETIER_AFTER` there.","files":null}]}